# WHAT VERCEL UPLOADS.
#
# Without this file Vercel uploads the whole repository on every deploy, and
# references/experiments alone is 695 MB of evidence screenshots that neither
# the app nor the reader ever opens. That is what exceeded the size limit.
#
# Nothing listed here is deleted. The evidence stays in git and stays published;
# it just stops being shipped to the edge.
#
# What the deployment actually needs:
#   app/          the server and app/public (the build's source, and
#                 api/tree.js includeFiles reads app/public/{index,404}.html)
#   api/ lib/     the functions and their helpers
#   prototype/    src/ is copied to public/tree; compare.html is rewritten
#   tools/        build-static.mjs runs at build time
#   analysis/     lib/ and probe/ only — see below
#   package.json package-lock.json vercel.json

# Evidence archive: published in the repo, useless to the running app.
references/

# Prose.
docs/
*.md
!README.md

# Tests run in CI and locally, never on the edge.
test/

# The reader's captured screenshots and run output. api/grow.js imports only
# analysis/lib/analyze.js, which pulls in probe/{measure,pixels,accent-regions}
# and lib/mapping.js. The scripts that read shots/ and results/ are standalone
# CLI tools that never run in a function.
analysis/shots/
analysis/results/
analysis/node_modules/

# Build output. ANCHORED: unanchored, `public/` also matches `app/public/`,
# which is the build's SOURCE — excluding it took the homepage and every static
# asset to 404. Same trap as the .gitignore entry that once refused
# `git add app/public/...`. tools/build-static.mjs regenerates /public itself.
/public/

# Local only.
node_modules/
.git/
